#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "How to set up custom roles that provide access to a specific set of actions"
msgstr "Paano mag-set up ng custom na mga role na nagbibigay ng access sa isang tiyak na hanay ng mga aksyon"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Set up custom roles"
msgstr "Mag-set up ng custom na mga role"

#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Set up custom roles {#set-up-custom-roles}"
msgstr "Mag-set up ng custom na mga role {#set-up-custom-roles}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When account owners and administrators set up user access for an account, they assign roles (example: Editor, Viewer, Operator, and so on) to [access policies and access groups](/guides/access-groups), and then assign users to those policies or groups. A user can perform all the actions mapped to the role or roles that have been assigned to their access group or policy.\n"
msgstr "Kapag nag-set up ang mga may-ari ng account at mga administrator ng user access para sa isang account, nagtatalaga sila ng mga role (halimbawa: Editor, Viewer, Operator, at iba pa) sa [mga access policy at access group](/guides/access-groups), at pagkatapos ay itinatakda ang mga user sa mga policy o group na iyon. Maaaring gawin ng isang user ang lahat ng aksyong naka-mapa sa role o mga role na itinalaga sa kanilang access group o policy.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In addition to the pre-configured roles listed on the [Roles](https://cloud.ibm.com/iam/roles) page, account owners and administrators can create roles that better match their needs. For example, you can create a custom role that grants a user access to view account usage analytics without granting any other management access. The next section gives a step-by-step demonstration of this example.\n"
msgstr "Bukod sa mga pre-configured na role na nakalista sa pahina ng [Roles](https://cloud.ibm.com/iam/roles), maaaring lumikha ang mga may-ari ng account at mga administrator ng mga role na mas angkop sa kanilang mga pangangailangan. Halimbawa, maaari kang lumikha ng custom na role na nagbibigay sa isang user ng access para tingnan ang analytics ng paggamit ng account nang hindi nagbibigay ng anumang iba pang access sa pamamahala. Ang susunod na seksyon ay nagbibigay ng sunud-sunod na demonstrasyon ng halimbawang ito.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"custom\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"custom\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Example: create a custom role that allows users to perform actions to work with IBM Quantum service instances {#example-create-a-custom-role-that-allows-users-to-perform-actions-to-work-with-ibm-quantum-service-instances}"
msgstr "Halimbawa: lumikha ng custom na role na nagpapahintulot sa mga user na magsagawa ng mga aksyon para sa IBM Quantum service instances {#example-create-a-custom-role-that-allows-users-to-perform-actions-to-work-with-ibm-quantum-service-instances}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This custom role grants quantum-specific roles to users.\n"
msgstr "Ang custom na role na ito ay nagbibigay ng mga quantum-specific na role sa mga user.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "From [Manage → IAM → Roles](https://cloud.ibm.com/iam/roles), click `Create`.\n"
msgid "From [Manage → IAM → Roles](https://cloud.ibm.com/iam/roles), click `Create` (only visible for account administrators).\n"
msgstr "Mula sa [Manage → IAM → Roles](https://cloud.ibm.com/iam/roles), i-click ang `Create`.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "Enter a name, ID, description, and select `Qiskit Runtime` for the service.\n"
msgid "Enter a name, ID, description, and select `Quantum Compute` for the service.\n"
msgstr "Maglagay ng pangalan, ID, paglalarawan, at piliin ang `Qiskit Runtime` para sa serbisyo.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Select the following roles, then click **Create**.\n"
msgstr "Piliin ang mga sumusunod na role, pagkatapos ay i-click ang **Create**.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    * '
#, no-wrap
msgid "quantum-computing.device.read\n"
msgstr "quantum-computing.device.read\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    * '
#, no-wrap
msgid "quantum-computing.job.cancel\n"
msgstr "quantum-computing.job.cancel\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    * '
#, no-wrap
msgid "quantum-computing.job.create\n"
msgstr "quantum-computing.job.create\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    * '
#, no-wrap
msgid "quantum-computing.job.read\n"
msgstr "quantum-computing.job.read\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    * '
#, no-wrap
msgid "quantum-computing.program.delete\n"
msgstr "quantum-computing.program.delete\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    * '
#, no-wrap
msgid "quantum-computing.program.read\n"
msgstr "quantum-computing.program.read\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    * '
#, no-wrap
msgid "quantum-computing.user.logout\n"
msgstr "quantum-computing.user.logout\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    * '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Select quantum-computing.job.delete if you want to allow users to delete jobs.\n"
msgstr "Piliin ang quantum-computing.job.delete kung gusto mong payagan ang mga user na mag-delete ng mga job.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Example: create a custom role for a user to view analytics only {#example-create-a-custom-role-for-a-user-to-view-analytics-only}"
msgstr "Halimbawa: lumikha ng custom na role para sa isang user para tingnan lamang ang analytics {#example-create-a-custom-role-for-a-user-to-view-analytics-only}"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "Go to [Manage → IAM → Roles](https://cloud.ibm.com/iam/roles) in IBM Cloud. Select the Qiskit Runtime service from the dropdown menu to see the roles that currently exist for this service.\n"
msgid "Go to [Manage → IAM → Roles](https://cloud.ibm.com/iam/roles) in IBM Cloud. Select Quantum Compute from the dropdown menu to see the roles that currently exist for this service.\n"
msgstr "Pumunta sa [Manage → IAM → Roles](https://cloud.ibm.com/iam/roles) sa IBM Cloud. Piliin ang serbisyong Qiskit Runtime mula sa dropdown na menu para makita ang mga role na kasalukuyang mayroon para sa serbisyong ito.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Click the **Create +** button.\n"
msgstr "I-click ang button na **Create +**.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Enter a name for the custom role, such as `Analytics Viewer`.\n"
msgstr "Maglagay ng pangalan para sa custom na role, tulad ng `Analytics Viewer`.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Enter an ID. You can input any unique string for this ID, as long as it starts with a capital letter, and contains only alphanumeric characters (no spaces) - for example, `AnalyticsViewer`.\n"
msgstr "Maglagay ng ID. Maaari kang mag-input ng anumang natatanging string para sa ID na ito, basta magsisimula ito sa isang malaking titik, at naglalaman lamang ng mga alphanumeric na karakter (walang espasyo) — halimbawa, `AnalyticsViewer`.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '5. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Enter a description for the custom role. In this example, an appropriate description might be \"As an Analytics Viewer, you can view account analytics only.\"\n"
msgstr "Maglagay ng paglalarawan para sa custom na role. Sa halimbawang ito, ang angkop na paglalarawan ay maaaring \"Bilang isang Analytics Viewer, maaari kang tingnan ang analytics ng account lamang.\"\n"

#. type: Bullet: '6. '
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "In the Service dropdown menu, choose Qiskit Runtime. A table appears that contains all the actions that you can map to the role.\n"
msgid "In the Service dropdown menu, choose Quantum Compute. A table appears that contains all the actions that you can map to the role.\n"
msgstr "Sa dropdown na menu ng Service, piliin ang Qiskit Runtime. Lilitaw ang isang talahanayan na naglalaman ng lahat ng aksyong maaari mong i-mapa sa role.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"7. For this example, look for any actions that pertain to analytics, such as \"Read usage filters for analytics\" and \"Read usage for analytics\". Also include the \"Read account configuration\" action.\n"
"To add the actions to your custom role, click Add at the end of the action's row.\n"
msgstr ""
"7. Para sa halimbawang ito, hanapin ang anumang mga aksyong may kaugnayan sa analytics, tulad ng \"Read usage filters for analytics\" at \"Read usage for analytics\". Isama rin ang aksyong \"Read account configuration\".\n"
"Para idagdag ang mga aksyon sa iyong custom na role, i-click ang Add sa dulo ng row ng aksyon.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '8. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Once you have added all the actions you want mapped to the role, click Create.\n"
msgstr "Kapag naidagdag mo na ang lahat ng aksyong gusto mong i-mapa sa role, i-click ang Create.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '9. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Go to [Manage → IAM → Access groups](https://cloud.ibm.com/iam/groups). Click **Create +** to create a new access role. (It is recommended to create a new access group especially for this role, rather than add the role to your Public Access group, unless you want all your users to have the access granted by your custom role.) Once you have clicked **Create +** and named your new group (or, in the case of editing an existing access group, once you have clicked the name of the access group to edit), then click the Access tab. Click **Assign access +**.\n"
msgstr "Pumunta sa [Manage → IAM → Access groups](https://cloud.ibm.com/iam/groups). I-click ang **Create +** para lumikha ng bagong access role. (Inirerekomenda na lumikha ng bagong access group lalo na para sa role na ito, kaysa idagdag ang role sa iyong Public Access group, maliban kung gusto mong lahat ng iyong mga user ay magkaroon ng access na ibinibigay ng iyong custom na role.) Kapag na-click mo na ang **Create +** at napangalanan ang iyong bagong group (o, sa kaso ng pag-edit ng isang kasalukuyang access group, kapag na-click mo na ang pangalan ng access group para i-edit), i-click ang tab na Access. I-click ang **Assign access +**.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '10. '
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "Under Service, select Qiskit Runtime, then click Next.\n"
msgid "Under Service, select Quantum Compute, then click Next.\n"
msgstr "Sa ilalim ng Service, piliin ang Qiskit Runtime, pagkatapos ay i-click ang Next.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '11. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Under Resources, select All resources, then click Next. (Note that if you do not scope the access to all resources, the Analytics Viewer role will not be able to see analytics from all instances.)\n"
msgstr "Sa ilalim ng Resources, piliin ang All resources, pagkatapos ay i-click ang Next. (Pansinin na kung hindi mo ililimitahan ang access sa lahat ng resources, hindi makikita ng Analytics Viewer role ang analytics mula sa lahat ng instance.)\n"

#. type: Bullet: '12. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Under Roles and actions, check the Viewer box (under Platform) and the Analytics Viewer box (under Custom access), then click Next.\n"
msgstr "Sa ilalim ng Roles and actions, lagyan ng tsek ang kahon ng Viewer (sa ilalim ng Platform) at ang kahon ng Analytics Viewer (sa ilalim ng Custom access), pagkatapos ay i-click ang Next.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '13. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Click **Add >**, then click Assign. You have now created a policy that includes your custom role as well as the Viewer role.\n"
msgstr "I-click ang **Add >**, pagkatapos ay i-click ang Assign. Nakagawa ka na ngayon ng isang policy na kinabibilangan ng iyong custom na role pati na rin ang Viewer role.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '14. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "View the access group, and click the Users tab to add a user to this group. This user will now be able to perform the actions in your custom role (as well as the other roles you assigned to the policy).\n"
msgstr "Tingnan ang access group, at i-click ang tab na Users para magdagdag ng user sa group na ito. Ang user na ito ay makakapagsagawa na ngayon ng mga aksyon sa iyong custom na role (pati na rin ang iba pang mga role na itinalaga mo sa policy).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To learn more, see the [Creating custom roles](https://cloud.ibm.com/docs/account?topic=account-custom-roles) and the [What are IAM policies and who can assign them?](https://cloud.ibm.com/docs/account?topic=account-iamusermanpol) topics.\n"
msgstr "Para matuto pa, tingnan ang mga paksa na [Creating custom roles](https://cloud.ibm.com/docs/account?topic=account-custom-roles) at [What are IAM policies and who can assign them?](https://cloud.ibm.com/docs/account?topic=account-iamusermanpol).\n"
